## 2. Section-by-section

Repeat per section. The value is in the **field-level diff**, not the verdict: "same requirement"
is only trustworthy when you can see the two clauses side by side.

**Assess at the unit the buyer gates independently.** A criterion with three separately-scored or
separately-page-capped sub-parts is three sections, not one — a flat verdict hides the sub-part
that moved. And a diff that feeds somewhere other than drafting (e.g. the Form-of-Contract
old-vs-new diff, which feeds the risk register) still gets its own `###` section, marked
*(informational)*.

### <section ref + title>
**Status:** FULL REUSABLE / PARTIAL / REQUIRES UPDATE / NEW · **Reuse:** <~%>
**Maps to:** R-0xx *(compliance-matrix row — reuse and compliance must agree)*

Go **element by element**, not section by section. "Section 4.1 is reusable" hides the one field
that moved; a table of elements makes the actual edit list fall out of the analysis.

| Element | Prior (`<PRIOR-ID>`) | Current ({{ENG_ID}}) | Where it lives in the prior response | Status |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| <e.g. turnover requirement> | <old value> | <new value> `[RFP §x]` | <doc + section> | Same / **CHANGED** / CHECK |

